+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to get multiple parts, largest unit first. Units run from days down to seconds, zero parts are skipped, and leftover milliseconds are dropped (so anything under 1 second gives `"0s"`). Output always uses short unit names; `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })          // "1s"
+ms(500, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
